{"title":"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 19","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A park is in the shape of a regular hexagon <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> km on a side. Starting at a corner, \nAlice walks along the perimeter of the park for a distance of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> km. \nHow many kilometers is she from her starting point?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/f/f1f33a4ba8ba3efde8c07d7bbf8af6f64023acf9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\sqrt{13}\\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ \\sqrt{14}\\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ \\sqrt{15}\\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ \\sqrt{16}\\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\sqrt{17}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"470\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We imagine this problem on a coordinate plane and let Alice's starting position be the origin. We see that she will travel along two edges and then go halfway along a third. Therefore, her new <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-coordinate will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/b/37b271ca08305fb9b71e08c2d7709957ebb02041.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 2 + \\frac{1}{2} = \\frac{7}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"111\" height=\"37\" /> because she travels along a distance of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/0/6000aa8e4fb9e28819ae985e0b0037aeb278353f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"67\" height=\"37\" /> km because of the side relationships of an equilateral triangle, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> km because the line is parallel to the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-axis, and the remaining  distance is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> km because she went halfway along and because of the logic for the first part of her route. For her <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-coordinate, we can use similar logic to find that the coordinate is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/f/91f826b18c8a193054b0759e2f7ce560e3605b82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{3} + 0 - \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} =  \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"157\" height=\"41\" />. Therefore, her distance is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/d/7ad22f1a96150a6c4b502c0e7667ccee8f75e297.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{7}{2}\\right)^2 + \\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)^2} = \\sqrt{\\frac{49}{4} + \\frac{3}{4}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{52}{4}} = \\sqrt{13},\\]\" width=\"375\" height=\"64\" /> giving an answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/e/f6eb65962292d994ce2f9a8af63728883f256b18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{A}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"27\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME\" title=\"1986 AHSME\">1986 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1986 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1986\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_P